WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
Here's a closed box.

2
00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:05.700
Twenty centimetres long,
twelve wide, nine tall.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.750
Lay a thin pencil along the longest edge.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.030
Twenty centimetres.

5
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.020
Easy.

6
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.790
Now swing it diagonally across the base.

7
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:14.970
That's longer.

8
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.400
Then tilt it up towards
the far top corner.

9
00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:23.350
So which placement wins, and how
long can the pencil actually be?

10
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.040
In this mission, you'll use
Pythagoras twice in a cuboid:

11
00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.930
once on the base, then
again with the height.

12
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.330
That gives you the distance formula
for any two points in three dimensions.

13
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.870
You'll also learn to spot the right-angled
triangle hidden inside a solid.

14
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.970
Your mission: work out the longest pencil
that fits in a twenty by twelve by nine

15
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.320
centimetre box.
